engine biome(1.0)
language js(typescript, jsx)

// A fleet-manager screen may not read a query's raw `isError`.
//
// React-query keeps `data` through a failed refresh, so "we hold an answer" and
// "the last attempt failed" are independent facts. A screen that branches on
// `isError` alone collapses them and states something false: it either deletes
// figures it still holds, or claims an empty fleet it was never told about. Six
// screens each invented their own answer to this before the disposition
// primitive existed.
//
// `useQueryDisposition` reads both facts and returns exactly four cases;
// `QuerySurface` renders them. A screen asks for a disposition and wraps its
// claims in the surface — it never reads the flag itself.
//
// Scope: `apps/fleet-manager/src/pages/**` (see the `includes` in biome.json).
// That is where a screen makes a claim about the fleet, and it is the app the
// primitive lives in — a rule may only require what exists. Feature components
// stay out on purpose: a *mutation's* `isError` is an action that failed, not a
// read the screen must dispose of, and banning it there would be a false alarm
// on every Save button in the app.
`$read.isError` as $flag where {
  register_diagnostic(span=$flag, message="A screen may not branch on a query's raw `isError`. Use `useQueryDisposition` for the screen's reads and render the claims through `QuerySurface`, so a failed refresh marks the data stale instead of deleting it. See operator-ui/packages/biome-plugins/README.md.", severity="error")
}
